<main class="info-page"><div class="info-inner info-legal">
<h1>About this banking demo</h1><p class="info-sub">Clear information about Willow’s status and simulated services.</p>
<section class="info-section" id="regulatory-status"><h2>A fictional banking experience</h2><p>Willow Banking Corp. is an educational software demonstration, not a licensed bank or a provider of real financial services. Creating a demo account does not open a real bank account. The app does not perform identity verification or regulatory screening.</p></section>
<section class="info-section" id="deposit-protection"><h2>Simulated funds only</h2><p>Account balances, deposits, withdrawals, transfers and cards are simulated records. The app does not accept, hold or move real money and is not connected to a bank or payment network. No deposit insurance or compensation scheme applies to these simulated balances.</p></section>
<section class="info-section" id="independent-review"><h2>No certification claims</h2><p>No independent audit report or security certification is provided for this demo. It does not claim SOC 2 certification, PCI DSS compliance or approval from a financial regulator. Implemented account protections are explained on the <a href="/security-info">security page</a>.</p></section>
<section class="info-section" id="demo-use"><h2>Exploring the app</h2><p>Use fictional names and contact details, and a password you do not use elsewhere. Business checking is a single-owner simulated account; no real business services are connected. Any real-world service would require its own verified operating status, disclosures and security review.</p></section>
</div></main><%- include('partials/public-footer') %></body></html>
